{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/2450-trinity-continuum-crossovers","id":2450,"title":"Trinity Continuum crossovers","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-04T00:08:20-08:00","id":2450,"title":"Trinity Continuum crossovers","content":"So: the Trinity Continuum core book will include a modern-day setting featuring Talents; \u00c6on will feature a century-from-now setting featuring psions. Presumably, Aberrant will be a day-after-tomorrow setting featuring Novas. Will these games be designed to be compatible with each other, system-wise? That is, if I want to include Talents in the Aberrant or \u00c6on settings, will I be able to use the Talents rules from the core book as is? If I want to include psychics in the Aberrant setting, will the rules suggest hacking the Aberrant mechanics to represent psi-powered characters, or will it point to \u00c6on's rules for psions, possibly with some tweaks to represent how psis of that era differ from psis of the later era?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T09:39:53-08:00","id":2693,"title":"","content":"The systems were always compatible, but they weren't balanced. A Nova is vastly stronger than a Psion and a Psion is typically more powerful than a Mesmerist. But they work about as well as different types of Exalted characters, I spose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a professor! Why is no one listening to me?!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/235-telgar","name":"Telgar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2506"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T12:06:04-08:00","id":2818,"title":"","content":"As Telgar said, they were compatible, perhaps not cleanly so though.<br /> <br /> On a semi-related note - If we really have to go down the route of mixing things up so the era and power type are essentially interchangeable, I'd like to at least see that done without compromising the tone and themes of the different periods. Aberrants (end of the War era and out to 2120s) should be much more powerful than, say Psions. If the history is relatively intact in the new edition then the War was won only through the threat of a scorched earth policy, not because humanity could actually 'win' (or even come close to it). in 2102 humanity is (rightly) terrified that Psions won't be up to the challenge of taking down the Colony or Mal and the hordes of space crazy abbies.<br /> <br /> One of the things that drew me to Trinity was that the bad guys were such a potentially overwhelming threat. Then again, I intensely dislike crunchy overpowered PC's in a game, probably one of the reasons I'm not that big a fan of Aberrant as it was published. I suspect from what's been said so far, there will be a measure of interchangeability between the three (and potentially other) periods - that makes sense commercially let alone mechanically.<br /> <br /> I just hope it can be done without having to spend too much time undoing such rule for those of us that, for example, want to avoid A! and Aberrant era powers showing up in Trinity. I have a hunch the dev's will figure out a middle ground. This topic seems to come up frequently enough I doubt the devs aren't aware of various desires to mix, and keep distinct, the different periods/powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 11-05-2013, 11:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-04T16:40:42-08:00","id":3007,"title":"","content":"I very much hope that they make the systems more cleanly interchangable. My pipe dream is to run a modern game of emergent superhumans and/or talents in a world slowly going strange, while the Psion enforcers of the Doyen/Illithids/Greys are trying to keep things enshrouded in secrecy and eliminate these growing threats to The Timetable. I have faith in Ian's ability to make this a reality.<br /> <br /> ..okay, that was a bit much, but you get my meaning. I'm agreeing with the sentiment that system interoperability will likely be A Thing in the forthcoming continuum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/720-rubio","name":"Rubio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar720_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T08:07:42-08:00","id":3495,"title":"","content":"Lol, yeah I get what you mean.<br /> <br /> It certainly seems from the handful of comments from devs about this (an RPG.net thread IIRC, could be wrong) they've got it covered in a way that allows heavy blending and keeping things separate, as the GM desires - plus allowing them to add more periods, which is exciting.<br /> <br /> Now, just don't get me started on Process 418 as it panned out in Trin V1, bleh. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":232,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","user":"CHILL","date":". 11-05-2013, 11:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T08:11:31-08:00","id":3503,"title":"","content":"Oh, please <i>do</i> get started; I\u2019d like to hear it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T08:35:15-08:00","id":3520,"title":"","content":"Must....resist..... OK, willpower fail.<br /> <br /> For me, 418 as written in Terra Verde felt a lot like it was trying to tie the three game settings / mechanics together - to wrap things up. The game mechanics didn't work well together, and it felt a bit, well, crunchy to me. I'd been perfectly happy with Trinity before Ab or A! arrived, without any blending of A! or Ab power types into it - so this just felt like a wasted opportunity. If I wanted to GM/play supers or heroic types then those game books / settings were available, no need to bring that stuff to the Trinity setting and (just my opinion) dilute/muddle Trinity further. I respect that other people love the idea of crossovers, though, even if I don't.<br /> <br /> I've been a huge Trinity fan since the first book (Aeon, damnit!), and less so Ab or A! as anything other than backstory for Trin*. So, my perspective is going to be very different from someone who prefers those games or wants (for example) 22nd century high supers or psions in the 1920s. As mentioned elsewhere, if we get a toolkit allowing GMs to avoid doing a bucketload of work to keep things separate OR opting to run crossover games without compromising the tone of the settings then I'll be extremely happy.<br /> <br /> Just getting new books for Trinity does it for me in any event <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <i>*I do own several copies of each of the books for all three lines, and have GMd and played all of them. I just prefer Trin out of the three as it hits all my buttons, so to speak. I will more than likely buy anything that comes out for 2nd Ed Ab and A! as well as Trin, as I'm sure they'll be a great read just like the v1's were/are, even if I find they're not my kind of thing to run/play.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#ff0000\"><b>Ad Astra</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/232-chill","name":"CHILL","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar232_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T10:00:58-08:00","id":3582,"title":"","content":"I like the idea of the three line working better together, but I've always crossed classes from the three lines with each other. I do think that the Continuum would be served by a more consistent rule set, and clearly defined rules for how things interact. I never liked building Abberants for Trinity by giving them versions of Psion powers. I've always used Aberrant rules for the Abberants in my Trinity games. But, if the system were designed from the beginning to support that, I'd be pleased as punch. So, I'm excited to see where Continuum 2.0 takes us. I feel the design of Adventure! was sublime, and those rules should be ported to the new system as directly as possible. The other two lines are where we hit a few issues. <br /> <br /> I don't have a problem with Aberrant characters being crazy powerful, but I want the feel to be right. I never felt that Taint was half as big a threat as the setting material makes it out to be. Nova characters should feel like a supercharged train engine that will go out of control and go off the rails at any moment. Novas should have to struggle to maintain control and avoid going taint mad. On the other had Psions should feel like the undisputed masters of their given spheres of influence. This doesn't require that Psions beable to out damage Novas/Aberrants with simular power. While Novas/Aberrants should be brute force like a hacksaw, Psions should embody precision like a scalpel.<br /> <br /> But that's just my take.<br /> <br /> -Slag","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6-slagheap","name":"Slagheap","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"188"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T11:59:46-08:00","id":3661,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'd like them to be kept separate due to the genre shifts between games. Two-fisted heroes with uncanny luck don't always groove well in a space opera (Capt Kirk and Han Solo notwithstanding), just as uber-powerful mutants and psychics would (usually) fall into the &quot;out of control problem of the week&quot; category in pulp adventures.<br /> <br /> Also, the on-going build-up of Z-particle/Quanta/(forgot what they are in Aeon) is a plot point for the entire line. The power levels should build up as time progresses forward. Extremely powerful novas and psions are woefully out of place in the A! era. The two exceptions are, of course, the most significant NPCs in the entire line.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T20:25:25-08:00","id":3970,"title":"","content":"My initial comment was based on inconsistencies that existed among the various gamelines in the Trinity Universe. Consider how each line handled psychic characters: <b>Trinity</b> had its Psi, Aptitudes, and Modes, and an assumption that baseline humans have Psi 1. <b>Aberrant</b> assumed that psychic characters would use reskinned Quantum Powers with some minor rules tweaks mostly concerning Taint. <b>Adventure!</b>\u2019s mesmerists used an ill-defined Inspiration trait and Psychic Knacks. The result was that the three games\u2019 respective versions of psychics felt like three radically different kinds pf things, not merely different stages of power with a few minor variations in some of the specifics. <br /> <br /> What I\u2019m hoping to see in the Trinity Continuum is a standard framework for handling psychic characters, with the different eras varying in terms of, say, which Techniques an <b>Adventure!</b>-era mesmerist has access to and/or how readily available Noetic Energy is. Different dials and switches on a common \u201cNoetic Powers\u201d engine, rather that completely different engines. I want <b>\u00c6on</b>-era Aberrants to use the same rules as <b>Aberrant</b>-era Novas, tweaked to allow for how much more serious of a problem Taint is in the <b>\u00c6on</b> era, and I want <b>Adventure!</b>\u2019s stalwarts to be mechanically identical to <b>Aberrant</b>\u2019s \u201cstealth Novas\u201d. I want Talents to work the same in all eras: baseline humans who are remarkably capable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T20:38:59-08:00","id":3974,"title":"","content":"Not to mention they never really decided if Daredevils were using any &quot;actual&quot; super powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T21:09:06-08:00","id":3986,"title":"","content":"Indeed. I\u2019m really hoping that they decide against it in the Trinity Continuum; if you want subconscious reality manipulators, that\u2019s what superhumans and psychics (probably psychics) are for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:52:03-08:00","id":4080,"title":"","content":"Word of Ian is that Talents can't become psions, or vice versa. He also has his own theory linking Talents, Max, and time travel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T22:56:27-08:00","id":4083,"title":"","content":"Oh? Where is this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T23:19:27-08:00","id":4104,"title":"","content":"They're both from the same thread; <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?699376-White-Wolf-Onyx-Path-Gen-Con-spoilers&amp;p=17098648#post17098648\" target=\"_blank\">here's his statement about them being non-interchangeable</a> (he also mentions that while Talents won't get explicit support in Aeon, there's nothing stopping you using them in the game) and <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?699376-White-Wolf-Onyx-Path-Gen-Con-spoilers&amp;p=17102391#post17102391\" target=\"_blank\">here's where he mentions having a theory</a>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?699376-White-Wolf-Onyx-Path-Gen-Con-spoilers&amp;p=17102166#post17102166\" target=\"_blank\">This post may also be relevant.</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-05T23:33:25-08:00","id":4106,"title":"","content":"<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:courier new\">The specifics of Talents, Mercer, and time travel are a sticky wicket. I've got my own conception on exactly how they all function. I fully expect not everyone will be happy, but I think most will.</span></div> This doesn\u2019t sound like \u201cI have a theory that ties them all together\u201d; though that <i>is</i> one possible interpretation of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-06T09:16:51-08:00","id":4393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/2450-trinity-continuum-crossovers?p=4104#post4104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're both from the same thread; <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?699376-White-Wolf-Onyx-Path-Gen-Con-spoilers&amp;p=17098648#post17098648\" target=\"_blank\">here's his statement about them being non-interchangeable</a> (he also mentions that while Talents won't get explicit support in Aeon, there's nothing stopping you using them in the game) and <a href=\"http://forum.rpg.net/showthread.php?699376-White-Wolf-Onyx-Path-Gen-Con-spoilers&amp;p=17102391#post17102391\" target=\"_blank\">here's where he mentions having a theory</a>.<br /> <br /> <a 